**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** One file per entry: write it, then read it back through schema, version and hash checks (001 §B: 'One entry per file', 'Every entry file carries', 'JSON Schema per kind', 'No up-converters'; .spec-md §5). (1) `Errors.fs`: `StorageError` (`:21-27`) gains `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr of SchemaVersionMismatchInfo` and `ContentHashMismatchErr of ContentHashMismatchInfo`. The two records are declared above it: `SchemaVersionMismatchInfo = { fileExtension : FileExtension; found : FileSchemaVersion; expected : FileSchemaVersion }`, where the extension names the file's kind (001 §A) so that S4's kit files can reuse the case, and `ContentHashMismatchInfo = { entryId : LibraryEntryId; recorded : ContentHash; computed : ContentHash }`. Records carry the two same-typed fields, because a case holding them as a tuple is ELEV011. The doc list (`:11-20`) names both cases. No existing match on `StorageError` is exhaustive, so no consumer changes. (2) Schemas, in draft 2020-12 like `schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json`, each with its own `$id` (`https://berreman/schema/library-<kind>.json`). `schema/library-common.schema.json` holds, once, the definitions that every entry and the catalogue share: the GUID string, a positive version, the content hash `^[0-9a-f]{64}$` and the four provenance shapes. The others reference it by its `$id`. `schema/library-material.schema.json`, `library-sample`, `library-source`, `library-polarizer`, `library-detector` and `library-category` each describe exactly what this step's writer emits for their kind. Each checks unconditionally that `schema` is `{ kind: <the kind's tag>, version: <a positive integer> }`. Everything else is checked only under `if` `schema.version` is 1 (`then`): every key present and no other (`additionalProperties: false`); `id` a GUID; `name` a non-empty string; `categoryOpt` a GUID for a material and `null` otherwise; `descriptionOpt` a string for a sample, a string or `null` for a material, and `null` otherwise; `payload` the kind's case tag with its record's required keys; `provenance` one of the four shapes; and `contentHash` the hash pattern. The physics inside a payload (`MaterialComplexity`, `SampleStructure`, `PolarizerBehavior`, `SourceTuning`) is bound by the serializer, which reports a malformed one as `MalformedJsonErr`. A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. Each file is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest`, beside the existing `schema/optical-constructor-*.schema.json` items of `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no new comment. (3) `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `type LibraryEntryKind with member schemaFile : FileName` (`schema/library-<kind>.schema.json`); the common schema and one lazy per kind, each loaded once (`JsonSchema.FromText` registers an `$id` only once, `:17-21`), with the common schema loaded before any entry schema evaluates; and `validateEntry (kind : LibraryEntryKind) (element : JsonElement)` over step 29's `validateWith`. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs`, `module EntryFileJson`, compiled directly after `CanonicalJson.fs`. `LibraryFileText of string` is a library file's text, UTF-8 without a BOM; S2's database payload and S4's kit snapshot hold it byte for byte. `LibraryEntryContent.sealed : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` is the content with `contentHashOf content` (step 27). `LibraryEntryEnvelope.fileText : Result<LibraryFileText, StorageError>` is the content's canonical node with `contentHash` added beside its keys, rendered indented and ending with one `\n`; `ProjectJson.serializeProject` adds `schemaVersion` the same way. `LibraryFileText.parseEntry (kind : LibraryEntryKind) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` works in this order. It parses the text (`MalformedJsonErr`). It validates the document against the kind's schema (`SchemaValidationErr`), so a file of another kind fails here. It compares `schema.version` with `kind.currentSchemaVersion` before anything binds (`UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`). It binds the content from the document without `contentHash` (`MalformedJsonErr`). Finally it compares `contentHashOf content` with the recorded hash (`ContentHashMismatchErr`). There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Every .NET call that throws is caught here and mapped; nothing above handles an exception. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs` (`module EntryFileJsonTests`), appended to the compile list after `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs`. Each round trip goes content → `sealed` → `fileText` → `parseEntry` and answers an equal envelope, whose decoder answers the original value. (a) `a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape`: one constant complexity for each `ConstantEpsValue` case; dispersive complexities over `IsotropicDispersive`, `UniaxialDispersive` and `BiaxialDispersive` whose segments together carry every `EpsAxisDispersion` case: `RealNK` (through `DispersionModel.toEpsAxis` of a Cauchy model) and `ComplexEps` (of a Sellmeier model), `TabulatedNK` (through `TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate`), `TaucLorentzAxis`, `GaussianOscillatorAxis`, `ForouhiBloomerAxis` and `BrendelBormannAxis` (through `toEpsAxis` of coefficient sets written in the fixture), and `PublishedLawAxis` of each `PublishedIndexLaw`; one complexity with a constant and one with a dispersive `magnetic` aspect; and one with each `active` case, `RhoWithoutDispValue`, `RhoWithDispValue` and `PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw`. (b) `a multilayer sample entry file round-trips`: `SeedSamples.multilayerQw` (a `Repeated` period group) and `SeedSamples.langasiteSilicon`. (c) `a tunable source entry file round-trips`: a `SeedSources.tunables` source under `BuiltInProvenance` and a user source under `UserProvenance`. (d) `a constant-Mueller polarizer entry file round-trips`: a two-component `ConstantMueller` polarizer in the `CustomMueller` category. (e) `a detector and a category entry file round-trip`: the ellipsometer detector and the `standardCategories` Vacuum category. (f) `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`: one material under each of the four provenance cases. (g) `an entry file is indented canonical JSON whose hash survives a write and a read`: the text is the indented canonical rendering, ends with one `\n` and holds no `\r`; writing the parsed envelope again gives the same text; and the hash equals `contentHashOf` of the content. (h) `an entry file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: a material file with `schema.version` set to 2 answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = MaterialEntryKind.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`, both with its body intact and with `payload` replaced by `{}`. (i) `a tampered entry file is ContentHashMismatchErr`: a number inside the payload changed in the text, with the recorded hash kept, answers `ContentHashMismatchErr` whose `recorded` is the file's hash and whose `computed` is the changed content's. (j) `a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr`: the file without `name`, and a sample's file parsed as a material, answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; a text that is not JSON answers `MalformedJsonErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the entry files land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the ten EntryFileJsonTests facts from `a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape` to `a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.
